                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use the common tower height to find the ground distances, then find the angle at A and subtract it from the bearing of O from A.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "From the two vertical right triangles:\n$$\\begin{align*}OA&=\\frac{100}{\\tan15^\\circ}\\text{ m}\\\\OA&\\approx373.2051\\text{ m}\\\\OB&=\\frac{100}{\\tan10^\\circ}\\text{ m}\\\\OB&\\approx567.1282\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$\nLet $\\theta=\\angle OAB$. Using unrounded distances in the right-angled ground triangle:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{OB}{OA}\\\\\\theta&=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\tan15^\\circ}{\\tan10^\\circ}\\right)\\\\\\theta&\\approx56.6526^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nThe bearing of $O$ from $A$ is $290^\\circ$. Since $B$ lies north of $O$ and $\\angle AOB=90^\\circ$, the bearing of $B$ from $O$ is $020^\\circ$.\nUsing the unrounded value of $\\theta$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Bearing of }B\\text{ from }A&=290^\\circ-\\theta\\\\&\\approx233.3473654^\\circ\\\\&\\approx233.3^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
